cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Minimum Wage Difference-in-Differences Study: 2021 State Increases and Food Service/Retail Employment"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Pareddy
    given-names: Charith Reddy
repository-code: "https://github.com/Charith-Reddy-Pareddy/min-wage-difference-in-differences-study"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A difference-in-differences study of 2021 state minimum wage increases and
  employment in food service and retail, with an exposure-gradient hypothesis,
  inference and robustness checks, and a Python machine learning and causal ML
  extension. The R pipeline is the study's identification strategy; the Python
  package is an exploratory extension and makes no claim beyond that.
keywords:
  - difference-in-differences
  - minimum wage
  - econometrics
  - reproducible research
